- op: discuss  # a51e
  at: '2026-03-20T23:56:33Z'  # a51e
  by: agent  # a51e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a51e
  clock: 2  # a51e
  nonce: a51e  # a51e
  message: "Bakeoff finding (deep-20260320-163609, tokenizers): Zero Rust<->Python cross-language edges despite PyO3 bindings (#[pyclass], #[pymethods]). The PyFFI linker exists but doesn't create edges for this repo. Need to investigate: (1) Are PyO3 annotations being detected by the Rust analyzer? (2) Does the linker run? (3) What matching criteria fail?"  # a51e
- op: discuss  # 487c
  at: '2026-03-21T00:00:05Z'  # 487c
  by: agent  # 487c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 487c
  clock: 3  # 487c
  nonce: 487c  # 487c
  message: "Root cause found: The Rust analyzer stores PyO3 attributes with name='pyo3' (the crate name), not 'pyfunction'/'pymethods'/'pyclass' (the specific attribute). The PyFFI linker checks for the specific names only. 809 of 1823 Rust symbols in tokenizers have pyo3 annotations. Fix: add 'pyo3' to _PYO3_ANNOTATIONS frozenset in pyffi.py."  # 487c
